        "procedure": "General procedure for 2a–2e: dibenzoylmethane (2.7 g, 12 mmol) and N-ethylpyrrolidine (1.5 mL, 12 mmol) were dissolved in ca. 80 mL of absolute ethanol and carefully heated to boiling. A solution of PrCl3·7H2O (1.15 g, 3 mmol) in a minimum of absolute ethanol was added. The clear solution was placed in a Dewar filled with boiling water and allowed to cool slowly to room temperature overnight. Apple-green crystals were isolated by filtration, washed with cold ethanol (ca. 20 mL), and dried in air.",
